{"name":"Malta","hex":"#a59784","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Malta","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An archipelago and country in Southern Europe, in the Mediterranean Sea. Official name: Republic of Malta. Capital: Valletta.","The largest island in the Maltese Archipelago."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Malta"}],"entries":[{"title":"Malta","blocks":[{"text":"Malta, officially the Republic of Malta, is an island country located in the central Mediterranean Sea. It consists of a number of islands, of which Malta and Gozo are the two main ones—south of Italy, east of Tunisia, and north of Libya. Valletta is the country's capital. Malta is the world's tenth-smallest country by area, ninth-most densely populated, and 166th most populated. It consists of a single urban region, because of which it is often described as a city-state. The two official languages are Maltese—recognised as the national language—and English."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Flag_of_Malta.svg/330px-Flag_of_Malta.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malta","wikidata":"Q233"},{"title":"Malta (island)","blocks":[{"text":"Malta is an island in Southern Europe. It is the largest and most populous of the three major islands that constitute the Maltese Archipelago and the country of Malta. The island is situated in the Mediterranean Sea directly south of Italy and north of Libya. It lies south-east of the smaller islands of Gozo and Comino. The island is 27 kilometres (17 mi) long and 14.5 kilometres (9 mi) wide, with a total area of 246 square kilometres (95 sq mi). The capital is Valletta, while the largest locality is Rabat. The island is made up of many small towns, which together form one larger urban zone with a population of 409,259. The landscape is characterised by low hills with terraced fields."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Malta_ali_2009224_lrg.jpg/330px-Malta_ali_2009224_lrg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malta_(island)","wikidata":"Q193896"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Templo_de_%C4%A0gantija%2C_isla_de_Gozo%2C_Malta%2C_2021-08-23%2C_DD_18.jpg/500px-Templo_de_%C4%A0gantija%2C_isla_de_Gozo%2C_Malta%2C_2021-08-23%2C_DD_18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Templo_de_%C4%A0gantija%2C_isla_de_Gozo%2C_Malta%2C_2021-08-23%2C_DD_18.jpg/1280px-Templo_de_%C4%A0gantija%2C_isla_de_Gozo%2C_Malta%2C_2021-08-23%2C_DD_18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Templo_de_%C4%A0gantija%2C_isla_de_Gozo%2C_Malta%2C_2021-08-23%2C_DD_18.jpg/500px-Templo_de_%C4%A0gantija%2C_isla_de_Gozo%2C_Malta%2C_2021-08-23%2C_DD_18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ġgantija, a megalithic temple complex","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATemplo_de_%C4%A0gantija%2C_isla_de_Gozo%2C_Malta%2C_2021-08-23%2C_DD_18.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Justinian555AD.png/500px-Justinian555AD.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Justinian555AD.png/1280px-Justinian555AD.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Justinian555AD.png/500px-Justinian555AD.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" The lands making up modern-day Malta was once a part of the Byzantine Empire (its vassals in pink).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wi